  "bodyText": "Youth\n\n“Rejoice in the Lord always. I will say it again: Rejoice! Let your gentleness be evident to all. The Lord is near.”\n\nPhilippians 4:4-5 (NIV)\n\nThe Youth Ministry at First Baptist delights in sharing the joy of the Lord with students grades 6-12. In this amazing and formative time in life, students are asking big questions about God, faith, and the world around them. The youth ministry hopes to encourage students to see their life within the great story of God’s faithfulness, love, and salvation in Christ Jesus.\n\nCheck out our regular online newsletter entitled “The Moose’s Message” to see the latest updates or contact the church for more information.\n\nSchedule\n\nLarge Group Meeting\n\nEvery Sunday, 9:30-10:15 a.m.\n(FBCM Youth Center)\n\nOur main teaching time where students gather at the intersection of God’s work and our lives. Pastor Jonathan and Kendall, alongside a youth volunteer, open up scripture and discuss how God’s work intersects with student’s lives.\n\nAfter Youth Large Group meetings, students typically attend Donut (Semi) Hour with the whole congregation (10:15-10:45 a.m.).\n\nFamily Day Out Events\n\nDiscipleship, maturity, studying scripture. All of those are important goals we have as a youth ministry. We also believe that all of that is fully compatible with having a whole lot of fun.\n\nThe FBCM Youth Ministry invites students to partake in \"Family Day Out\" events, as well as special youth events. From frisbee golf, to escape rooms, to Christmas parties, or any number of fun events – these are great opportunities to invite a friend and have a great time.\n\nYou can find more information at the newsletter, and even register for events using the church app.\n\nCity Life Club Meeting\n\nWednesdays During School Year\n\n7:17 - 8:45 p.m.\n(FBCM Fellowship Hall/\n\nYouth Center)\n\nFBCM is a site for \"City Life!\" All students grades 6 - 12 are welcome.\n\nWe begin with a meal at 7:17 p.m. in the fellowship hall.\n\nThen, we have some time for fun and games and end with a Bible study.\n\nOther Youth Events Include\n\nCamps\n\nRetreats\n\nMission Trips\n\nAll-Church Events\n\nServing as important leaders in Worship\n\nHelping to lead Vacation Bible School\n\nGet Involved\n\nIf you wish to be a part of our youth ministry, contact us!\n\nLorraine Garrett\n\nCCT Youth Coordinator\n\nyouth[at]fbcmuncie.org",
